Nexus (https://github.com/cnr-isti-vclab/nexus)
  Copyright (c) 2012-2020, Visual Computing Lab, ISTI - CNR. MIT licence ("All Javascript Nexus
  software is free and release under the MIT license").
  The traversal, the cache rule, the drawing of the nodes and the three.js object derive from
  html/js/nexus.js and html/js/nexus_three.js at commit d805432:
    src/math.js, src/priority-queue.js, src/instance.js, src/mesh.js, src/context.js,
    src/gl-upload.js, src/bm3d-object.js.
  What was changed: ES modules in place of globals, and three.js as an import; the new header,
  index and metadata of the bm3d format (src/format.js, written from docs/FORMAT.md, replaces the
  Nexus parser); HTTP Range requests with fetch and an optional cache (IndexedDB); the corto decoder
  as a module worker that loads corto.wasm from a path the host gives; no meco, deep zoom or point
  rendering; no RGBFormat or VertexColors; vertex colours are unsigned bytes; nodes that are dropped
  while loading are not uploaded; a corrupt node or texture is reported and not asked for again.
  Two fixes were made first to the copy of Nexus that the DroneDB Hub shipped, and are carried
  here: the error of a node is measured in the pixels of the drawing buffer (getDrawingBufferSize),
  not in CSS pixels, and textures are minified with LINEAR_MIPMAP_LINEAR and up to 8x anisotropic
  filtering.

corto (https://github.com/cnr-isti-vclab/corto)
  Copyright (c) 2015-2022, Visual Computing Lab, ISTI - CNR. MIT licence.
  corto.wasm is the decoder of corto, at commit d240e69306a39417c098475d7002eb16b7264248 with the
  patches of third_party/corto-patches/ of the bm3d repository, built with emscripten from
  corto-wasm/emcorto.cpp (derived from html/js/emscripten/emcorto.cpp) and corto-wasm/build.sh
  (derived from html/js/emscripten/build.sh). src/corto-worker.js derives from the decoding
  function of html/js/emscripten/corto.em.proto.js.

three.js is a peer dependency and is not part of this package.
